  "description": "I would like to erect a poly tunnel on the 1.21 ha of land that I lease from the owners of Douglas Eyre Sports Centre (the London Playing Fields Association). Dimensions of the polytunnel are 8m (w) x 14m (l) x 3m (h). The polytunnel would be aluminium frame with polythene covering. The tunnel would be soley used to grow flowers. The site is screened by trees and shrubbery which would conceal the polytunnel structure from the nearest residential buildings (500m away).\nThe land I rent is located to the west of the Douglas Eyre playing fields sandwiched between the reservoirs and the Dagenham Brook and the flood attenuation channel.\nThe land is used for horticulure growing flowes for sale to florists and local residents. The site has historically been used for agricultural activity, until 1914 is was part of a Walthamstow farm, Elm farm, when it was acquired by the London Playing Fields Association. The site was seperated from the playing fields in 1968 by the construction of a flood channel, Since that time the site has been used for the grazing of animals, hence its address, Grazing Land adjacent to Douglas Eyre Playing Fields. The site has been a flower farm since March 2020. The land is leased by the London Flower Farmer  from  its owner the LPFA for the sole use of growing flowers. This planning application is supportered by the landowners, see attached letter.",
